    "end": "They argued about the sprouts.",
    "caption": "Liz has her back to the in-laws, for now.\n\nIsla: 4.6 million people, a 23-hour day, one moon, and a coastline that changes with everyone's moods. A cross word puts a puddle between you. A proper falling-out puts in a sea. Maps are printed in pencil. Liz and her in-laws hadn't spoken since Easter, over a borrowed lawnmower, or possibly a seating plan. Then December came round, and somebody had to sort out Christmas.\n\nI muted a group chat. There's a ferry now.\n\n(On Earth, the sea covers about seven-tenths of the planet, which explains a lot about Christmas.)\n\nHow wide is your sea at the moment?"
  },
